  "blocks": {
    "\"Bypass permissions?\"": "“使用<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent-mode\">绕过权限</a>模式？”",
    "\"I'm running this AFK — three sandboxed agents on the refactor, reviewing the PRs in the morning.\"": "“我要让它 AFK 运行——三个沙箱化智能体并行处理重构，明早再审查 PR。”",
    "\"Yeah, read-only filesystem, no network.\"": "“对，但<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/filesystem\">文件系统</a>只读，而且禁止联网。”",
    "Avoid: \"background agent\" — centers the machine (\"running in the background\") rather than the human pattern (\"user has walked away\"). AFK names the fact that matters: the user isn't watching.": "<em>避免：</em>称为“后台智能体”。这个说法关注机器“在后台运行”，而不是人“已经离开”的工作模式。AFK 直接点明真正重要的事实：用户没有在旁观察。",
    "Away from keyboard. A working pattern where the user kicks off a session and leaves the agent to run unattended. The throughput multiplier of AI coding — many AFK sessions can run in parallel while you sleep, eat, or work on something else. Usually requires a permissive permission mode plus sandboxing to be safe.": "AFK 是 Away From Keyboard（离开键盘）的缩写，指用户启动一次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>后离开，让<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>在无人值守的情况下继续运行。这是 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/ai\">AI</a> 编码的吞吐量倍增器：当你睡觉、吃饭或处理其他工作时，可以并行运行多个 AFK 会话。为了安全，通常需要较宽松的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/permission-mode\">权限模式</a>与<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/sandbox\">沙箱</a>配合。",
    "Since you can't give input during the run, give it before and after instead. Before: resolve the ambiguity up front — a grilling session, a written spec — so there are fewer gaps for the agent to fill alone. During: automated checks and automated review stand in for the attention you're not giving, failing fast on what can be caught mechanically. After: the run ends in something reviewable — a PR, not changes already merged. AFK doesn't remove human review; it defers all of it to the end, which is why what arrives at the end has to be worth reviewing. This is also why AX matters most in AFK runs — with no one watching, the environment is the only support the agent gets.": "由于运行期间无法提供输入，就应把指导放在运行前后。运行前：通过一次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/grilling\">深度追问</a>会话或书面<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/spec\">规格说明</a>预先解决歧义，减少智能体独自填补的空白。运行中：用<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-check\">自动化检查</a>和<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-review\">自动化审查</a>代替你未能投入的注意力，让可以机械发现的问题尽快失败。运行后：最终产物必须可供审查——应当是 PR，而不是已经合并的改动。AFK 并不会取消<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/human-review\">人工审查</a>，只是把审查全部推迟到最后，因此最终到达的产物必须值得审查。这也是 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/ax\">AX</a> 在 AFK 运行中最重要的原因：无人观察时，环境是智能体能够获得的唯一支持。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "When you're not there, the agent handles ambiguity differently. While you're watching, an ambiguous decision surfaces as a question and you answer it; once you've walked away, the agent picks a default and keeps going, and every later decision builds on that guess. The characteristic failure is coming back to hours of finished, confident work built on a wrong call made in the first ten minutes. The work isn't sloppy — it's coherent, just coherent about the wrong thing.": "当你不在场时，智能体处理歧义的方式会发生变化。你在旁观察时，模糊决策会以问题形式浮现，并由你回答；你一旦离开，智能体就会选择一个默认答案继续前进，后续每个决定都建立在这次猜测上。典型失败是：回来后发现它已经自信地完成了数小时工作，但全部建立在前十分钟作出的错误判断之上。工作本身并不潦草，逻辑甚至十分连贯，只是围绕了错误目标保持连贯。"
  },
